      "This condition impairs the heart's ability to pump blood effectively to the rest of the body.",
      "It may manifest as enlargement, thickening, or stiffening of the heart chamber walls.",
      "Causes range from genetic mutations and viral infections to chemical toxins.",
      "Patients often present with dyspnea, chronic fatigue, and lower extremity edema.",
      "Diagnosis frequently involves echocardiography to assess wall motion and pumping capacity.",
      "It can lead to severe complications such as arrhythmias or congestive heart failure.",
      "The dilated form is characterized by left ventricular enlargement with systolic dysfunction.",
      "The restrictive form features impaired diastolic filling due to fibrosis or infiltrative disease.",
      "The hypertrophic form involves increased thickness of the left ventricular wall, potentially obstructing outflow."
